(Chandra-ruled — Chandra enemy of Shani); Mrigashira, Chitra, Dhanishtha
(Mangala-ruled — Mangala enemy of Shani)

#strong[This is a notable prediction]: many of the nakshatras most
favorable for gold (Surya-ruled) and silver (Chandra-ruled) are
#emph[least] favorable for iron operations. The
Surya/Chandra/Mangala-ruled nakshatras are problematic for iron.
#emph[Iron has the most antagonistic friendship pattern of any single
dhatu.]

This may have practical consequence: traditional smelting and forging
operations could specifically be timed to favor Saturn-favorable
nakshatras (those ruled by Saturn-friendly grahas: Mercury and Venus,
plus neutral Jupiter). This is testable through analysis of any
historical records of iron production timing if such records exist.

=== 5.3 Iron-mercury operations (lauha-bhasma marana when Hg-mediation
is used)
<iron-mercury-operations-lauha-bhasma-marana-when-hg-mediation-is-used>
Some lauha-bhasma protocols use mercury-mediated kajjali; others use
only triphala-kvatha. For mercury-mediated protocols:

Two-graha (Shani + Budha). Shani-Budha is #emph[friend] both directions.
Framework predicts strong favorability across many nakshatras: -
#strong[Most favorable]: Aslesha, Jyeshtha, Revati (Budha-ruled, both
grahas favor); Pushya, Anuradha, Uttara Bhadrapada (Shani-ruled, both
grahas favor) - #strong[Moderate]: most other nakshatras except those
ruled by Surya/Chandra/Mangala - #strong[Avoid]:
Surya/Chandra/Mangala-ruled nakshatras (still antagonistic to iron-Shani
even though favorable to Mercury-Budha)

This is one of the more restrictive prediction sets in the dhatu
compendium because Shani’s enmities create wide swaths of unfavorable
nakshatras.

=== 5.4 Iron operations using triphala-kvatha (no mercury)
<iron-operations-using-triphala-kvatha-no-mercury>
The classical preferred method for lauha-bhasma uses only triphala
without mercury. This is single-graha (Shani only) and follows the §5.2
prediction pattern.

#strong[For most-favorable timing of triphala-mediated lauha-bhasma
operations, classical practitioners would optimally schedule on Mercury
or Venus-ruled nakshatras (Aslesha, Jyeshtha, Revati, Bharani, Purva
Phalguni, Purva Ashadha) or Saturn’s own nakshatras (Pushya, Anuradha,
Uttara Bhadrapada).]

This is a derivable framework prediction. Comparison against classical
murti-pratishtha-list (Volume on panchaloha analysis): of these
predicted-favorable nakshatras, Pushya, Anuradha, Uttara Bhadrapada are
in the classical pratishtha list; Aslesha, Jyeshtha, Revati, Bharani,
Purva Phalguni, Purva Ashadha are #emph[not]. The framework prediction
for iron operations diverges noticeably from the general murti
pratishtha list — #emph[because iron operations have different
graha-priorities than multi-metal sacred alloys].

=== 5.5 Iron in panchaloha/ashtadhatu
<iron-in-panchalohaashtadhatu>
The framework’s structural validation analysis (91.7% precision/recall
for ashtadhatu) treats iron as one of eight equal-weighted components.
Iron’s contribution to the multi-metal analysis is significant precisely
because Shani’s enmities create constraints that the other components
don’t have.

For ashtadhatu specifically: the optimal nakshatras must avoid extreme
conflict with Shani while supporting all other components. This is what
makes the structural validation finding (91.7%) so robust — the
framework correctly handles the tension between iron-Shani’s enmities
and the other grahas’ friendships.

